# Daily Driver Workspace

This directory is a [daily-driver](https://github.com/skoonin/daily-driver) workspace.
It holds your personal context, task tracker, {% if "job_search" in plugins %}job search data, {% endif %}and Claude session scaffolding.

## Day-to-day commands

```
daily-driver day-start        # open a Claude session to plan your day
daily-driver check-in         # mid-day check-in with Claude
daily-driver day-end          # close-out session and capture learnings
```

## Task tracker

```
daily-driver tracker add      # add a task ({% if "job_search" in plugins %}job, {% endif %}errand, milestone, etc.)
daily-driver tracker list     # list tracked tasks
daily-driver tracker update   # update status or notes on a task
daily-driver tracker stats    # summary counts by status/category
```

{% if "job_search" in plugins %}
## Job search

```
daily-driver jobs run              # run configured job board scrapers
daily-driver jobs discover-boards  # find Greenhouse, Ashby, and Lever boards that list your roles
daily-driver jobs backfill         # fill empty fields in jobs.csv rows
daily-driver jobs promote          # copy a jobs.csv row into the tracker
daily-driver jobs status           # show last-run metadata per source
daily-driver jobs prune            # archive stale rows from jobs.csv
daily-driver jobs verify           # close saved jobs that are no longer posted
```

{% endif %}
## Status and focus

```
daily-driver status           # dashboard table (Rich or --json)
daily-driver focus on         # suppress check-ins while deep-focused
daily-driver focus off        # re-enable check-ins
```

## Maintenance

```
daily-driver doctor           # verify workspace integrity
daily-driver doctor --fix     # repair drift, preserve your edits
daily-driver doctor --reset   # repair drift, overwrite managed files
```

## Configuration

Edit `.dd-config.yaml` in this directory to configure categories, {% if "job_search" in plugins %}job sources, {% endif %}daily schedule, and other workspace settings.

## Managed files

Files under `.claude/commands/daily-driver/`, `.claude/agents/daily-driver/`, and `.claude/hooks/` are package-managed. After a version upgrade, `doctor` reports drift, and `doctor --fix` refreshes them:

- It keeps your edits to shipped files.
- It deletes `.md` files you added to `.claude/commands/daily-driver/` or `.claude/agents/daily-driver/`, and `.sh` files you added to `.claude/hooks/`. Put your own commands in `.claude/commands/user/`.
- It replaces the allow rules saved in `.claude/settings.local.json`.

`doctor --reset` wipes those directories and rewrites them from the installed package, so your edits and added files there are lost.

This `README.md` is also package-managed and follows the same lifecycle.
